  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.5.0:\n- NEW: AddPrimusIdentityForAzureAD() one-liner for Azure AD / Microsoft Entra ID setup (handles v1.0 and v2.0 issuers).\n- NEW: Swagger/OpenAPI integration via AddPrimusSwagger() - auto-configures security definitions.\n- NEW: Enhanced dev-mode diagnostics with AddPrimusDevDiagnostics() and MapPrimusDevDiagnostics() endpoints.\n- NEW: PrimusDiagnosticsOptions for configuring detailed error messages, debug headers, and failure tracking.\n- NEW: AuthFailureTracker for tracking recent authentication failures with categorized reasons.\n- IMPROVED: SourceLink enabled for step-through debugging in consuming applications.\n- IMPROVED: Deterministic builds for reproducible packages.\n- IMPROVED: Comprehensive XML documentation on all new public types.\n\nv1.4.0:\n- NEW: .NET 9.0 / ASP.NET Core 9.0 support with Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.JwtBearer 9.0.11.\n- UPDATED: .NET 8.0 JwtBearer bumped to 8.0.22 (latest patch).\n- DOCS: Framework compatibility table and JWT bearer version pins clearly documented.\n- DOCS: Added modern minimal API integration guidance and samples.\n\nv1.3.6:\n- E2E tested: All 11 endpoint tests passing in real-world scenarios.\n- Verified API accuracy: PrimusIdentityLoggingOptions, claim mapping, multi-issuer validation.\n- Production-ready with comprehensive copy-paste code samples.\n\nv1.3.5:\n- DOCS: Comprehensive documentation update with accurate implementation examples and best practices.\n- Improved developer experience with copy-paste ready code samples.\n\nv1.3.4:\n- FEATURE: Expose matched issuer/provider via HttpContext.GetMatchedIssuer() and inject provider claims for downstream responses.\n- DOCS: Clarified Azure AD client_credentials issuer format (sts.windows.net) vs v2.0 and added guidance/examples.",
